# identity (step 10) — same treatment as .sniper-token/config.toml above.
# identity.db holds hashed/encrypted secrets, not plaintext, but the file
# itself is still never meant to leave this machine (session rows alone
# are enough to hijack an admin session if the DB leaked). The -wal/-shm
# siblings are SQLite's WAL-mode journal files; they can contain the same
# data as the main file mid-transaction and must never be committed either.
identity.db
identity.db-wal
identity.db-shm
.session-key
